 ],
 "literal": "Diverting from ruinous things, guiding in the right path, and sharing the suffering at the time of ruin is friendship.",
 "translation": "True friendship is that which diverts one from ruinous paths, guides them along the path of virtue, and shares in their suffering when misfortune strikes.",
 "modern": "தீய வழியிலிருந்து விலக்கி, நல்வழியில் செலுத்தி, துன்பம் வரும்போது உடன் இருந்து அந்தத் துன்பத்தைப் பகிர்ந்துகொள்வதே நட்பாகும்.",
 "explanation": "This couplet defines the active duties of a true friend. A real friend does not stand by idly; they actively steer one away from harmful paths and actions that lead to ruin. They then direct and guide one toward the path of virtue and goodness. Finally, if misfortune or ruin does strike, a true friend does not abandon them but stays to endure and share the grief and suffering.",
